# Project agent layout

- Skills live in `.cursor/skills/` (version-controlled). Activate the matching skill when working in that domain.
- Project rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (version-controlled). Follow every rule whose globs cover files you are about to change.
- Do not recreate `.agents/skills` or `.ai/rules` for this project. If Boost regenerates skills under `.agents/`, move them into `.cursor/skills/` and prefer `.cursor`.
- `composer require` / `composer update` must **not** run `boost:update`. That command stays out of `post-update-cmd`. Run `php artisan boost:update` only when a human deliberately wants Boost's stock guidelines or skills refreshed, then review the diff before committing.
- Never run `php artisan boost:install`. Boost is installed already; the installer rewrites `AGENTS.md` and Boost-listed skills from scratch. `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` both say so, because the stock Laravel README section still tells agents to run it.
- **`AGENTS.md` has two halves.** Boost owns everything between `<laravel-boost-guidelines>` and `</laravel-boost-guidelines>` and replaces that region wholesale on every `boost:update`. The `# Michicast House Rules` section below the closing marker is hand-written and is preserved. Put project guidance there, never inside the block. `boost.json` keeps `"guidelines": true` precisely because the split makes regeneration safe.
- `BOOST_RULES_ENABLED=false` in `.env` / `.env.example` suppresses Boost's `## Project Rules` section, which would otherwise tell agents to use `.ai/rules`. This project uses `.cursor/rules` instead.
- **Never hand-edit a Boost-provided skill.** `infer-conventions`, `laravel-best-practices`, `testing-best-practices` and `tailwindcss-development` are copied fresh from the package on every update, so any edit is silently reverted. `boost.json`'s `skills` array is regenerated *output*, not an input filter — removing a name from it does not protect the file. When stock skill text is wrong for this project, override it from `.cursor/rules` instead, the way `cruddy-by-design.mdc` overrides `laravel-best-practices`.
- House-owned skills (`ship-issue`, `create-github-issue`) are not Boost skills and are never touched. Keep them out of `boost.json`'s `skills` array so Boost's stale-skill pruning cannot delete them.
- Durable project decisions belong in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` with YAML frontmatter (`description`, `globs`, `alwaysApply`). Prefer that over Boost `record-rule` / `.ai/rules`.
- **Overrides the stock `infer-conventions` skill:** record discovered conventions as `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files, never under `.ai/rules`, and do not call the `record-rule` MCP tool. Read existing `.mdc` rules, not `.ai/rules/index.md`, when checking which dimensions are already covered.
- Local MCP secrets stay in `.cursor/mcp.json` (gitignored). `composer setup` copies it from `.cursor/mcp.example.json`; the GitHub PAT still has to be filled in by hand.
